 ## Setup
 
 1. If you do not already have it, download the latest [`hwaccel.ml.yml`][hw-file] file and ensure it's in the same folder as the `docker-compose.yml`.
-2. In `immich-machine-learning`, add one of -[armnn, cuda, ggml, rocm, openvino, rknn] to the `image` section's tag at the end of the line.
+2. In `immich-machine-learning`, add one of -[armnn, cuda, ggml, rocm, openvino, rknn] to the `image` section's tag at the end of the line. (The `-mnn` tag is not a hardware backend: it runs the facial recognition models on the CPU through MNN, which is 2-3x faster than ONNX Runtime for them on Arm CPUs, and needs no `extends` entry.)
